<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends easier on dollar demand.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends easier on dollar demand.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka lost its edge to close mostly weaker at 42.2400/42.2450 to the dollar in interbank trading on Tuesday compared with the previous 42.2350/42.2450.</p>
<p>Dealers said the taka eased on higher deamnd for dollars from importers after opening firmer at 42.2325/42.2425.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates closed unchanged at 5.0 percent to 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
</text>
